Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:03:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] dt-bindings: nvme: apple,nvme-ans: Add M4+ (t8132) and
 t6050 compatibles

Starting with M4 (t8132) the ANS ADT node carries an "nvme-secure-bar"
property and ten reg entries: the NVMMU registers stay at reg[3] (the
"nvme" window on M1-M3) while the NVMe registers moved to reg[9].  This
cannot be described with the existing two-entry binding, so add an
optional third "nvmmu" reg entry, required for apple,t8132-nvme-ans2,
and add apple,t6050-nvme-ans2 (M5 Pro/Max) with t8132 as fallback.

t6050 has two storage PCIe links like t6000/t6020 (PMGR devices
APCIE_SYS_ST0 and APCIE_SYS_ST1 in the ADT), so it takes three power
domains.

Evidence: m1n1 commit 53f8ee9b54ba ("nvme: support T8132", AsahiLinux/
m1n1 PR #652, MIT-licensed at tag v1.9.9) for the register split; ADT of
a Mac17,6 (J716c): /arm-io/ans has nvme-secure-bar, nvme-interrupt-idx = 4
and reg[3] = 0x21dcc0000 (+0x60010), reg[9] = 0x25dcc0000 (+0x10000).

Status: untested; dt_binding_check pending.

NOT FOR UPSTREAM SUBMISSION: AI-generated local research draft (Asahi
Linux generative-AI policy).  No Signed-off-by on purpose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
